    "review::.::holistic::incomplete_migration::collections_forcelegacy_test_seam": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::incomplete_migration::collections_forcelegacy_test_seam",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 2,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "Production collection readers take a test-only forceLegacy flag and choose a Dart path by row-count probe.",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "incomplete_migration",
        "related_files": [
          "lib/services/library/library_collections_database.dart",
          "test/library_collections_database_read_test.dart"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "readDatabaseSnapshot(...) and readDatabasePlaylistTracks(...) both declare bool forceLegacy = false (library_collections_database.dart lines 230 and 308).",
          "The gate `!forceLegacy && (nativeJobRunner != null || PlatformBridge.supportsCoreBackend)` plus a LIMIT 64 probe decides at runtime whether the native or the Dart reader runs, so the same query can take different paths depending on data size.",
          "The only callers passing forceLegacy: true are in test/library_collections_database_read_test.dart (lines 153, 166, 359); no production caller uses it."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Remove forceLegacy from the production signatures. Have the tests call the Dart reader through a dedicated test-only function or a constructor-injected reader, and keep one production read path per platform so the 64-row probe is not a behavioural switch.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "20b40f2a"
      },
